IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vrsa-core`

-- Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 (NSW), Part 4, with the Victims Rights and Support Regulation 2019 -- the Victims
-- Support Scheme from the seat of the victim applying for support.
--
-- SEAT: the victim applying for support: a primary, secondary or family victim, or the parent, step-parent or guardian
-- caring for a child primary victim (and anyone applying on a victim's behalf, who answers for the victim). "Am I a
-- victim? Am I excluded? What can I get, and how much? Which recognition payment? How much counselling? By when must I
-- apply?" Every question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in
-- vrsa-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule. The same fact has the
-- same input name and wording in every question, so a form can ask it once.
--
-- EDITION: act-2013-037 and sl-2019-0398, both version 2025-02-01, from the Open Australian Legal Corpus as at
-- 10 March 2025. NOT THE CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT; IT MAY BE OUT OF DATE.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims Support Scheme (NSW) -- the victim's questions`

-- The act, from the victim's answers (ss 19, 19A, 19AB, 25(2)-(2B)). One answer, "it injured or killed someone it was
-- directed at", serves both s 19(1)(c) and s 19A(1)(c).
GIVEN `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved violent conduct against someone`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `it injured or killed someone it was directed at`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `it happened in New South Wales`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `charges have been laid against the alleged offender`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident`                                IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was the intentional killing of the person who died`                            IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone has been charged with murder for the death`                               IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was a terrorist act`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The act`
`the act from my answers` `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` `it involved violent conduct against someone` `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` `it happened in New South Wales` `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` `someone has been charged with murder for the death` `it was a terrorist act` MEANS
    `The act` WITH
        `apparently occurred in the course of the commission of an offence`                         IS `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence`
        `involved violent conduct against one or more persons`                                      IS `it involved violent conduct against someone`
        `resulted in injury or death to one or more of those persons`                              IS `it injured or killed someone it was directed at`
        `was committed in New South Wales`                                                          IS `it happened in New South Wales`
        `apparently occurred in the course of an offence or other conduct constituting modern slavery` IS `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery`
        `involved subjecting one or more persons to slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child`  IS `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child`
        `resulted in injury or death to one of the persons subjected to it`                        IS `it injured or killed someone it was directed at`
        `involved a motor vehicle and caused the death of another person`                          IS `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death`
        `charges have been laid against the alleged offender`                                      IS `charges have been laid against the alleged offender`
        `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, and an offence has apparently occurred` IS `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred`
        `took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident`                             IS `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident`
        `took the form of the intentional killing of the primary victim`                           IS `it was the intentional killing of the person who died`
        `a person has been charged with murder in relation to the death`                           IS `someone has been charged with murder for the death`
        `was a terrorist act`                                                                       IS `it was a terrorist act`

-- The person, from the victim's answers (ss 20-25).
GIVEN `I was injured as a direct result of it`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen`                               IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person was under 18 when it happened`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `I committed it`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone died as a result of it`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `my relationship to the person who died`                                             IS A `Relationship to the person who died`
      `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who died is the alleged offender`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim I am applying for has since died`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was committing an offence when it happened`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The person`
`me from my answers` `I was injured as a direct result of it` `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen` `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards` `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed` `that person was under 18 when it happened` `I committed it` `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured` `someone died as a result of it` `my relationship to the person who died` `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` `the person who died is the alleged offender` `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime` `the victim I am applying for has since died` `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it` `I was committing an offence when it happened` `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened` `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me` MEANS
    `The person` WITH
        `was injured as a direct result of the act`                                               IS `I was injured as a direct result of it`
        `was injured trying to prevent the act, help or rescue a person, or arrest the offender`  IS `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender`
        `was injured as a direct result of witnessing the act`                                    IS `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen`
        `was injured as a direct result of subsequently becoming aware of the act`                IS `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards`
        `is the parent or guardian of the primary victim`                                         IS `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed`
        `the primary victim was under 18 at the time of the act`                                  IS `that person was under 18 when it happened`
        `committed the act`                                                                       IS `I committed it`
        `is a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child who is a primary victim`         IS `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured`
        `a person died as a result of the act`                                                    IS `someone died as a result of it`
        `relationship to the person who died`                                                     IS `my relationship to the person who died`
        `had cohabited with the person who died for at least 2 years`                             IS `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years`
        `the person who died is the alleged offender`                                             IS `the person who died is the alleged offender`
        `is also a member of the immediate family of another person who died as a result of the road crime` IS `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime`
        `the victim has died`                                                                     IS `the victim I am applying for has since died`
        `has been paid, is entitled to, or has applied for court compensation under Part 6`       IS `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it`
        `was engaged in behaviour constituting an offence when the act occurred`                  IS `I was committing an offence when it happened`
        `was imprisoned as a convicted inmate when the act occurred`                              IS `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened`
        `the Commissioner is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception`           IS `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me`

§§ `ss 19 to 25 -- is it covered, am I a victim, am I excluded`

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, is what happened an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 ss 19, 19A, 19AB)?
GIVEN `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what happened apparently occurred while someone was committing a criminal offence (it counts even if that person could not be held criminally responsible because of their age or a mental illness or impairment)
      `it involved violent conduct against someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved violent conduct against one or more people; violent conduct includes sexual assault and domestic violence
      `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it injured or killed one or more of the people it was directed at; an injury is actual bodily harm, grievous bodily harm, or psychological or psychiatric harm, but not harm from loss of or damage to property
      `it happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was committed in New South Wales
      `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it apparently occurred in the course of an offence or other conduct that is modern slavery under the Modern Slavery Act 2018
      `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved subjecting someone to slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child (Crimes Act 1900 s 93AB)
      `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved a motor vehicle and caused another person's death
      `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether charges have been laid against the alleged offender for an offence in relation to it
      `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether charges cannot be laid because the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but on the balance of probabilities an offence apparently occurred
      `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it took the form of a motor accident, or the injury arose from one (motor accident as in the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999)
      `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was the intentional killing of the person who died
      `someone has been charged with murder for the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person has been charged with murder in relation to the death
      `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a terrorist act within the meaning of the Terrorism (Police Powers) Act 2002
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of act`
`what kind of act is it` `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` `it involved violent conduct against someone` `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` `it happened in New South Wales` `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` `someone has been charged with murder for the death` `it was a terrorist act` MEANS
    `the kinds of` (`the act from my answers` `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` `it involved violent conduct against someone` `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` `it happened in New South Wales` `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` `someone has been charged with murder for the death` `it was a terrorist act`)

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, am I a primary, secondary or family victim (or a carer of a child primary victim), and am I excluded (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 ss 20 to 25)?
GIVEN `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what happened apparently occurred while someone was committing a criminal offence (it counts even if that person could not be held criminally responsible because of their age or a mental illness or impairment)
      `it involved violent conduct against someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved violent conduct against one or more people; violent conduct includes sexual assault and domestic violence
      `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it injured or killed one or more of the people it was directed at; an injury is actual bodily harm, grievous bodily harm, or psychological or psychiatric harm, but not harm from loss of or damage to property
      `it happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was committed in New South Wales
      `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it apparently occurred in the course of an offence or other conduct that is modern slavery under the Modern Slavery Act 2018
      `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved subjecting someone to slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child (Crimes Act 1900 s 93AB)
      `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved a motor vehicle and caused another person's death
      `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether charges have been laid against the alleged offender for an offence in relation to it
      `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether charges cannot be laid because the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but on the balance of probabilities an offence apparently occurred
      `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it took the form of a motor accident, or the injury arose from one (motor accident as in the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999)
      `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was the intentional killing of the person who died
      `someone has been charged with murder for the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person has been charged with murder in relation to the death
      `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a terrorist act within the meaning of the Terrorism (Police Powers) Act 2002
      `I was injured as a direct result of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or the victim you are applying for) were injured as a direct result of it
      `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured as a direct result of trying to prevent it, trying to help or rescue someone it was being or had just been committed against, or trying to arrest the person committing it
      `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured (including psychological or psychiatric harm) as a direct result of witnessing it
      `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured (including psychological or psychiatric harm) as a direct result of becoming aware of it afterwards
      `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed
      `that person was under 18 when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person it injured or killed was under 18 at the time
      `I committed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you committed it
      `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child who was injured by it
      `someone died as a result of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone died as a result of it (for an act of violence, as a direct result)
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship to the person who died` @desc Your relationship, at the time it happened, to the person who died: spouse; de facto partner; parent, guardian or step-parent; child; step-child, or a child of whom they were the guardian; brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister, step-brother or step-sister; another relative; or no family relationship
      `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were their de facto partner: whether you had lived together for at least 2 years
      `the person who died is the alleged offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a road crime: whether the family member of yours who died is the alleged offender
      `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a road crime: whether you are also in the immediate family of another person who died as a result of it
      `the victim I am applying for has since died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are applying on behalf of a primary or family victim: whether that victim has died (answer no if you are applying for yourself)
      `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been paid, are entitled to be paid, or have applied for compensation awarded by a court for it under Part 6 of the Act
      `I was committing an offence when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened while you were engaged in behaviour constituting an offence
      `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened while you were imprisoned as a convicted inmate (answer no if you were in prison only for not paying a fine or other pecuniary penalty)
      `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were a convicted inmate: whether the Commissioner of Victims Rights is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception (serious and permanent injury may be one)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Victim status`
`am I a victim, and am I excluded` `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` `it involved violent conduct against someone` `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` `it happened in New South Wales` `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` `someone has been charged with murder for the death` `it was a terrorist act` `I was injured as a direct result of it` `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen` `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards` `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed` `that person was under 18 when it happened` `I committed it` `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured` `someone died as a result of it` `my relationship to the person who died` `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` `the person who died is the alleged offender` `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime` `the victim I am applying for has since died` `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it` `I was committing an offence when it happened` `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened` `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me` MEANS
    `the victim statuses of`
        (`the act from my answers` `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` `it involved violent conduct against someone` `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` `it happened in New South Wales` `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` `someone has been charged with murder for the death` `it was a terrorist act`)
        (`me from my answers` `I was injured as a direct result of it` `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen` `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards` `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed` `that person was under 18 when it happened` `I committed it` `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured` `someone died as a result of it` `my relationship to the person who died` `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` `the person who died is the alleged offender` `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime` `the victim I am applying for has since died` `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it` `I was committing an offence when it happened` `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened` `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me`)

§§ `ss 26 to 30A -- what support I can get`

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, what support am I eligible for, and up to what amounts (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 ss 26 to 30A; Victims Rights and Support Regulation 2019 cl 10 to 12)?
GIVEN `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what happened apparently occurred while someone was committing a criminal offence (it counts even if that person could not be held criminally responsible because of their age or a mental illness or impairment)
      `it involved violent conduct against someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved violent conduct against one or more people; violent conduct includes sexual assault and domestic violence
      `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it injured or killed one or more of the people it was directed at; an injury is actual bodily harm, grievous bodily harm, or psychological or psychiatric harm, but not harm from loss of or damage to property
      `it happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was committed in New South Wales
      `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it apparently occurred in the course of an offence or other conduct that is modern slavery under the Modern Slavery Act 2018
      `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved subjecting someone to slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child (Crimes Act 1900 s 93AB)
      `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved a motor vehicle and caused another person's death
      `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether charges have been laid against the alleged offender for an offence in relation to it
      `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether charges cannot be laid because the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but on the balance of probabilities an offence apparently occurred
      `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it took the form of a motor accident, or the injury arose from one (motor accident as in the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999)
      `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was the intentional killing of the person who died
      `someone has been charged with murder for the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person has been charged with murder in relation to the death
      `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a terrorist act within the meaning of the Terrorism (Police Powers) Act 2002
      `I was injured as a direct result of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or the victim you are applying for) were injured as a direct result of it
      `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured as a direct result of trying to prevent it, trying to help or rescue someone it was being or had just been committed against, or trying to arrest the person committing it
      `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured (including psychological or psychiatric harm) as a direct result of witnessing it
      `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured (including psychological or psychiatric harm) as a direct result of becoming aware of it afterwards
      `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed
      `that person was under 18 when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person it injured or killed was under 18 at the time
      `I committed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you committed it
      `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child who was injured by it
      `someone died as a result of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone died as a result of it (for an act of violence, as a direct result)
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship to the person who died` @desc Your relationship, at the time it happened, to the person who died: spouse; de facto partner; parent, guardian or step-parent; child; step-child, or a child of whom they were the guardian; brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister, step-brother or step-sister; another relative; or no family relationship
      `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were their de facto partner: whether you had lived together for at least 2 years
      `the person who died is the alleged offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a road crime: whether the family member of yours who died is the alleged offender
      `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a road crime: whether you are also in the immediate family of another person who died as a result of it
      `the victim I am applying for has since died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are applying on behalf of a primary or family victim: whether that victim has died (answer no if you are applying for yourself)
      `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been paid, are entitled to be paid, or have applied for compensation awarded by a court for it under Part 6 of the Act
      `I was committing an offence when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened while you were engaged in behaviour constituting an offence
      `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened while you were imprisoned as a convicted inmate (answer no if you were in prison only for not paying a fine or other pecuniary penalty)
      `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were a convicted inmate: whether the Commissioner of Victims Rights is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception (serious and permanent injury may be one)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Support`
`what support can I get` `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` `it involved violent conduct against someone` `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` `it happened in New South Wales` `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` `someone has been charged with murder for the death` `it was a terrorist act` `I was injured as a direct result of it` `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen` `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards` `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed` `that person was under 18 when it happened` `I committed it` `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured` `someone died as a result of it` `my relationship to the person who died` `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` `the person who died is the alleged offender` `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime` `the victim I am applying for has since died` `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it` `I was committing an offence when it happened` `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened` `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me` MEANS
    `the support for`
        (`the act from my answers` `what happened apparently occurred in the course of a criminal offence` `it involved violent conduct against someone` `it injured or killed someone it was directed at` `it happened in New South Wales` `it apparently occurred in the course of modern slavery` `it involved slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child` `it involved a motor vehicle and caused someone's death` `charges have been laid against the alleged offender` `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, but an offence apparently occurred` `it was, or my injury arose from, a motor accident` `it was the intentional killing of the person who died` `someone has been charged with murder for the death` `it was a terrorist act`)
        (`me from my answers` `I was injured as a direct result of it` `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` `I was injured as a direct result of seeing it happen` `I was injured as a direct result of learning of it afterwards` `I am the parent or guardian of the person it injured or killed` `that person was under 18 when it happened` `I committed it` `I am a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child it injured` `someone died as a result of it` `my relationship to the person who died` `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` `the person who died is the alleged offender` `I am also immediate family of another person who died in the road crime` `the victim I am applying for has since died` `I have court compensation for it, or have applied for it` `I was committing an offence when it happened` `I was in prison as a convicted inmate when it happened` `the Commissioner has decided special circumstances justify an exception for me`)

-- The financial questions take the victim's class as given (the eligibility question answers it), and give the most
-- that may be paid. The Commissioner may pay less (s 44, out of scope).
@export As an eligible primary victim under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, how much financial assistance can I get for my immediate needs and economic loss (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 ss 26, 30(2); Regulation cl 10)?
GIVEN `my urgent expenses for my safety, health or wellbeing` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: expenses for treatment or other measures that had to be taken urgently, as a direct result of the act, to secure your safety, health or wellbeing
      `how much of those urgent expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those urgent expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, under insurance or under another agreement, arrangement, Act or law
      `I can show actual loss of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can demonstrate actual loss of earnings as a direct result of the act (for a carer: because of the need to care for the child)
      `my weekly rate of lost earnings under cl 9` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars a week: the rate of actual loss of earnings worked out under Regulation cl 9 (the pre-2012 Workers Compensation Act 1987 s 37 rate, indexed; it is not computed here)
      `the number of weeks of earnings I lost` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of weeks of actual loss of earnings
      `how much of my lost earnings is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of the lost earnings you have received, or are entitled to receive, from workers compensation, insurance or another scheme
      `my out-of-pocket expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: your out-of-pocket expenses as a direct result of the act (assessed only if you cannot show actual loss of earnings)
      `how much of my out-of-pocket expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those out-of-pocket expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, from another source
      `my medical and dental expenses not claimed as urgent expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: actual medical and dental expenses incurred (for a carer: the child's), other than those claimed as urgent expenses
      `how much of those medical and dental expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those medical and dental expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, from Medicare, health insurance or another source
      `my justice-related expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: expenses of criminal or coronial proceedings about the act, making statements to police, preparing victim impact statements and similar justice-related expenses
      `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those justice-related expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, from another source
      `my lost or damaged clothing and personal effects` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the loss of, or damage to, clothing or other personal effects worn or carried by the primary victim at the time of the act
      `how much of that clothing and those effects is paid for from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of that loss you have received, or are entitled to receive, from insurance or another source
      `the amount paid or approved to my parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the total already paid or approved to your parent, step-parent or guardian for their economic loss in caring for you (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Financial assistance`
`how much can I get as a primary victim` `my urgent expenses for my safety, health or wellbeing` `how much of those urgent expenses is paid from another source` `I can show actual loss of earnings` `my weekly rate of lost earnings under cl 9` `the number of weeks of earnings I lost` `how much of my lost earnings is paid from another source` `my out-of-pocket expenses` `how much of my out-of-pocket expenses is paid from another source` `my medical and dental expenses not claimed as urgent expenses` `how much of those medical and dental expenses is paid from another source` `my justice-related expenses` `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source` `my lost or damaged clothing and personal effects` `how much of that clothing and those effects is paid for from another source` `the amount paid or approved to my parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27` MEANS
    `the s 26 financial assistance for`
        (`Primary victim claim` WITH
            `immediate needs expenses`                                       IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my urgent expenses for my safety, health or wellbeing`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of those urgent expenses is paid from another source`
            `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`                        IS `I can show actual loss of earnings`
            `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`              IS `my weekly rate of lost earnings under cl 9`
            `weeks of actual loss of earnings`                               IS `the number of weeks of earnings I lost`
            `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`              IS `how much of my lost earnings is paid from another source`
            `out-of-pocket expenses`                                         IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my out-of-pocket expenses`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of my out-of-pocket expenses is paid from another source`
            `medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs`     IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my medical and dental expenses not claimed as urgent expenses`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of those medical and dental expenses is paid from another source`
            `justice related expenses`                                       IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my justice-related expenses`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source`
            `clothing and personal effects`                                  IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my lost or damaged clothing and personal effects`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of that clothing and those effects is paid for from another source`
            `paid or approved to the parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27` IS `the amount paid or approved to my parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27`)

@export As a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child who is an eligible primary victim under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, how much can I get for economic loss (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 ss 27, 30(2); Regulation cl 11)?
GIVEN `I can show actual loss of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can demonstrate actual loss of earnings as a direct result of the act (for a carer: because of the need to care for the child)
      `my weekly rate of lost earnings under cl 9` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars a week: the rate of actual loss of earnings worked out under Regulation cl 9 (the pre-2012 Workers Compensation Act 1987 s 37 rate, indexed; it is not computed here)
      `the number of weeks of earnings I lost` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of weeks of actual loss of earnings
      `how much of my lost earnings is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of the lost earnings you have received, or are entitled to receive, from workers compensation, insurance or another scheme
      `my out-of-pocket expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: your out-of-pocket expenses as a direct result of the act (assessed only if you cannot show actual loss of earnings)
      `how much of my out-of-pocket expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those out-of-pocket expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, from another source
      `my medical and dental expenses not claimed as urgent expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: actual medical and dental expenses incurred (for a carer: the child's), other than those claimed as urgent expenses
      `how much of those medical and dental expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those medical and dental expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, from Medicare, health insurance or another source
      `my justice-related expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: expenses of criminal or coronial proceedings about the act, making statements to police, preparing victim impact statements and similar justice-related expenses
      `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those justice-related expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, from another source
      `my lost or damaged clothing and personal effects` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the loss of, or damage to, clothing or other personal effects worn or carried by the primary victim at the time of the act
      `how much of that clothing and those effects is paid for from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of that loss you have received, or are entitled to receive, from insurance or another source
      `the amount paid or approved to the child for economic loss under s 26(1)(c)` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the total already paid or approved to the child for the child's own economic loss (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Financial assistance`
`how much can I get as a carer of a child primary victim` `I can show actual loss of earnings` `my weekly rate of lost earnings under cl 9` `the number of weeks of earnings I lost` `how much of my lost earnings is paid from another source` `my out-of-pocket expenses` `how much of my out-of-pocket expenses is paid from another source` `my medical and dental expenses not claimed as urgent expenses` `how much of those medical and dental expenses is paid from another source` `my justice-related expenses` `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source` `my lost or damaged clothing and personal effects` `how much of that clothing and those effects is paid for from another source` `the amount paid or approved to the child for economic loss under s 26(1)(c)` MEANS
    `the s 27 financial assistance for`
        (`Carer claim` WITH
            `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`                        IS `I can show actual loss of earnings`
            `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`              IS `my weekly rate of lost earnings under cl 9`
            `weeks of actual loss of earnings`                               IS `the number of weeks of earnings I lost`
            `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`              IS `how much of my lost earnings is paid from another source`
            `out-of-pocket expenses`                                         IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my out-of-pocket expenses`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of my out-of-pocket expenses is paid from another source`
            `the child's medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs` IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my medical and dental expenses not claimed as urgent expenses`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of those medical and dental expenses is paid from another source`
            `justice related expenses`                                       IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my justice-related expenses`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source`
            `the child's clothing and personal effects`                      IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my lost or damaged clothing and personal effects`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of that clothing and those effects is paid for from another source`
            `paid or approved to the child under s 26(1)(c)`                 IS `the amount paid or approved to the child for economic loss under s 26(1)(c)`)

@export As an eligible family victim of an act of violence under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, how much can I get for immediate needs, the funeral and justice-related expenses (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 29; Regulation cl 12)?
GIVEN `my urgent expenses for my safety, health or wellbeing` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: expenses for treatment or other measures that had to be taken urgently, as a direct result of the act, to secure your safety, health or wellbeing
      `how much of those urgent expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those urgent expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, under insurance or under another agreement, arrangement, Act or law
      `the amount paid to someone else under s 47 for clean-up, taken from my urgent expenses amount` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: any amount the Commissioner has paid, or will pay, to a person who is not a family victim for cleaning up damage caused by the act, taken from your immediate needs amount (0 if none)
      `the funeral expenses I have paid or am likely to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the funeral expenses of the person who died that you have actually incurred or are reasonably likely to incur
      `the funeral expenses already granted to other family victims` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the funeral expenses already granted to other family victims for the same death (0 if none)
      `the amount paid to someone else under s 47 for the funeral` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: any amount paid, or to be paid, to a person who is not a family victim for the funeral (0 if none)
      `my justice-related expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: expenses of criminal or coronial proceedings about the act, making statements to police, preparing victim impact statements and similar justice-related expenses
      `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: how much of those justice-related expenses you have received, or are entitled to receive, from another source
GIVETH A `Family victim support`
`how much can I get as a family victim` `my urgent expenses for my safety, health or wellbeing` `how much of those urgent expenses is paid from another source` `the amount paid to someone else under s 47 for clean-up, taken from my urgent expenses amount` `the funeral expenses I have paid or am likely to pay` `the funeral expenses already granted to other family victims` `the amount paid to someone else under s 47 for the funeral` `my justice-related expenses` `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source` MEANS
    `the s 29 financial support for`
        (`Family victim claim` WITH
            `immediate needs expenses`                                       IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my urgent expenses for my safety, health or wellbeing`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of those urgent expenses is paid from another source`
            `amount payable under s 47 for clean-up, taken from immediate needs` IS `the amount paid to someone else under s 47 for clean-up, taken from my urgent expenses amount`
            `funeral expenses incurred or reasonably likely to be incurred`  IS `the funeral expenses I have paid or am likely to pay`
            `funeral expenses already granted to other family victims`       IS `the funeral expenses already granted to other family victims`
            `amount payable under s 47 for the funeral`                      IS `the amount paid to someone else under s 47 for the funeral`
            `justice related expenses`                                       IS `Expense` WITH `amount` IS `my justice-related expenses`, `paid or payable from another source` IS `how much of my justice-related expenses is paid from another source`)

@export I paid for the funeral of a person killed by an act of violence, or to clean up the damage it caused, and I am not a family victim: how much can I be reimbursed under the NSW Victims Support Scheme (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 47; Regulation cl 13)?
GIVEN `I am a family victim who can claim urgent or funeral expenses under s 29` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a family victim eligible for immediate needs or funeral expenses under s 29 (if so, claim them there)
      `the funeral expenses I paid for the person who died` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the reasonable expenses you incurred for the funeral of the person killed by the act of violence
      `the clean-up expenses I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the reasonable expenses you incurred cleaning up damage to premises and property caused as a direct result of the act of violence
      `the funeral expenses already granted to the family victims` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the funeral expenses already granted to family victims for the same death (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Section 47 answer`
`how much can I be reimbursed for the funeral or the clean-up` `I am a family victim who can claim urgent or funeral expenses under s 29` `the funeral expenses I paid for the person who died` `the clean-up expenses I paid` `the funeral expenses already granted to the family victims` MEANS
    `the s 47 reimbursement for`
        (`Section 47 claim` WITH
            `is eligible for immediate needs or funeral expenses under s 29 as a family victim` IS `I am a family victim who can claim urgent or funeral expenses under s 29`
            `funeral expenses of the primary victim incurred`                                IS `the funeral expenses I paid for the person who died`
            `clean-up expenses incurred`                                                     IS `the clean-up expenses I paid`
            `funeral expenses already granted to the family victims`                         IS `the funeral expenses already granted to the family victims`)

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, at what weekly rate is my actual loss of earnings worked out (Victims Rights and Support Regulation 2019 cl 9)?
GIVEN `I can show actual loss of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can demonstrate actual loss of earnings as a direct result of the act (for a carer: because of the need to care for the child)
GIVETH A `Weekly rate answer`
`what is my cl 9 weekly rate` `I can show actual loss of earnings` MEANS
    `the cl 9 weekly rate of actual loss of earnings` `I can show actual loss of earnings`

§§ `ss 34 to 36, 53 -- my recognition payment`

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, which recognition payment categories describe the act (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 35)?
GIVEN `it happened in the course of a homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act apparently occurred in the course of the commission of a homicide
      `it involved a sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved a sexual assault: sexual intercourse without consent (or with consent obtained by a non-violent threat), sexual intercourse with a child under 16 or a person with a cognitive impairment, compelled self-manipulation, or child prostitution or the use of a child for child abuse material
      `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury
      `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon
      `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sexual assault was carried out by 2 or more persons
      `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved sexual touching without consent, sexual touching of a child under 16, or a sexual act with or towards a child under 16
      `it involved an attempted sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved an attempted sexual assault
      `the attempted sexual assault involved violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attempted sexual assault involved violence
      `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attempted sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury
      `it involved an assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved an assault
      `the assault caused grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assault resulted in grievous bodily harm (including the destruction of the foetus of a pregnant woman)
      `it involved physical assault of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved physical assault of a child
      `it involved a robbery with violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved a robbery involving violence
      `it is one of a series of related acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is one of a series of related acts against the same person (committed at about the same time, or over time by the same person or group, or otherwise related), as the Commissioner or Tribunal sees it
GIVETH A LIST OF `Recognition category`
`which recognition categories describe the act` `it happened in the course of a homicide` `it involved a sexual assault` `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon` `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people` `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act` `it involved an attempted sexual assault` `the attempted sexual assault involved violence` `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `it involved an assault` `the assault caused grievous bodily harm` `it involved physical assault of a child` `it involved a robbery with violence` `it is one of a series of related acts` MEANS
    `the categories describing` (`the recognition facts from my answers` `it happened in the course of a homicide` `it involved a sexual assault` `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon` `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people` `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act` `it involved an attempted sexual assault` `the attempted sexual assault involved violence` `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `it involved an assault` `the assault caused grievous bodily harm` `it involved physical assault of a child` `it involved a robbery with violence` `it is one of a series of related acts`)

GIVEN `it happened in the course of a homicide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved a sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved an attempted sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attempted sexual assault involved violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved an assault` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assault caused grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved physical assault of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved a robbery with violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is one of a series of related acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Recognition facts`
`the recognition facts from my answers` `it happened in the course of a homicide` `it involved a sexual assault` `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon` `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people` `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act` `it involved an attempted sexual assault` `the attempted sexual assault involved violence` `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `it involved an assault` `the assault caused grievous bodily harm` `it involved physical assault of a child` `it involved a robbery with violence` `it is one of a series of related acts` MEANS
    `Recognition facts` WITH
        `apparently occurred in the course of the commission of a homicide`     IS `it happened in the course of a homicide`
        `involved a sexual assault`                                             IS `it involved a sexual assault`
        `the sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury`                  IS `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury`
        `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon`                       IS `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon`
        `the sexual assault was carried out by 2 or more persons`               IS `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people`
        `involved sexual touching or a sexual act`                              IS `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act`
        `involved an attempted sexual assault`                                  IS `it involved an attempted sexual assault`
        `the attempted sexual assault involved violence`                        IS `the attempted sexual assault involved violence`
        `the attempted sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury`        IS `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury`
        `involved an assault`                                                   IS `it involved an assault`
        `the assault resulted in grievous bodily harm`                          IS `the assault caused grievous bodily harm`
        `involved physical assault of a child`                                  IS `it involved physical assault of a child`
        `involved a robbery involving violence`                                 IS `it involved a robbery with violence`
        `is one of a series of related acts`                                    IS `it is one of a series of related acts`

@export As an eligible victim under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, which recognition payment is payable to me, how much is it, and is it suspended pending review (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 ss 36, 53; Regulation cl 14)?
GIVEN `it happened in the course of a homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act apparently occurred in the course of the commission of a homicide
      `it involved a sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved a sexual assault: sexual intercourse without consent (or with consent obtained by a non-violent threat), sexual intercourse with a child under 16 or a person with a cognitive impairment, compelled self-manipulation, or child prostitution or the use of a child for child abuse material
      `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury
      `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon
      `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sexual assault was carried out by 2 or more persons
      `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved sexual touching without consent, sexual touching of a child under 16, or a sexual act with or towards a child under 16
      `it involved an attempted sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved an attempted sexual assault
      `the attempted sexual assault involved violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attempted sexual assault involved violence
      `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attempted sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury
      `it involved an assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved an assault
      `the assault caused grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assault resulted in grievous bodily harm (including the destruction of the foetus of a pregnant woman)
      `it involved physical assault of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved physical assault of a child
      `it involved a robbery with violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involved a robbery involving violence
      `it is one of a series of related acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is one of a series of related acts against the same person (committed at about the same time, or over time by the same person or group, or otherwise related), as the Commissioner or Tribunal sees it
      `I was injured as a direct result of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or the victim you are applying for) were injured as a direct result of it
      `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured as a direct result of trying to prevent it, trying to help or rescue someone it was being or had just been committed against, or trying to arrest the person committing it
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship to the person who died` @desc Your relationship, at the time it happened, to the person who died: spouse; de facto partner; parent, guardian or step-parent; child; step-child, or a child of whom they were the guardian; brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister, step-brother or step-sister; another relative; or no family relationship
      `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were their de facto partner: whether you had lived together for at least 2 years
      `I was financially dependent on the person who died, immediately before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before the death, you were financially dependent on the person who died
      `I was under 18 immediately before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 immediately before the death (for a child of the person who died)
      `I was born after the death and would have been financially dependent on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a child of the person who died born after the death: whether you would have been financially dependent on them had you been born in their lifetime
      `I have already been given a recognition payment for another act in the same series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been given a recognition payment for another act in the same series of related acts against you
      `this act happened after support was given for the earlier act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this act happened after victims support was given for the earlier act (if so, it is not related to the earlier act)
      `I have applied to the Tribunal for review of the decision about my recognition payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to the Civil and Administrative Tribunal for review of a decision about the recognition payment
      `the Tribunal has ordered that my payment is not suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has ordered that payment go ahead despite the review
GIVETH A LIST OF `Recognition answer`
`which recognition payment do I get` `it happened in the course of a homicide` `it involved a sexual assault` `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon` `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people` `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act` `it involved an attempted sexual assault` `the attempted sexual assault involved violence` `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `it involved an assault` `the assault caused grievous bodily harm` `it involved physical assault of a child` `it involved a robbery with violence` `it is one of a series of related acts` `I was injured as a direct result of it` `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender` `my relationship to the person who died` `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years` `I was financially dependent on the person who died, immediately before the death` `I was under 18 immediately before the death` `I was born after the death and would have been financially dependent on them` `I have already been given a recognition payment for another act in the same series` `this act happened after support was given for the earlier act` `I have applied to the Tribunal for review of the decision about my recognition payment` `the Tribunal has ordered that my payment is not suspended` MEANS
    `the recognition payments for`
        (`the recognition facts from my answers` `it happened in the course of a homicide` `it involved a sexual assault` `the sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon` `the sexual assault was by 2 or more people` `it involved sexual touching or a sexual act` `it involved an attempted sexual assault` `the attempted sexual assault involved violence` `the attempted sexual assault caused serious bodily injury` `it involved an assault` `the assault caused grievous bodily harm` `it involved physical assault of a child` `it involved a robbery with violence` `it is one of a series of related acts`)
        `to`
        (`Recognition recipient` WITH
            `is a primary victim who suffered injury`                                       IS (`I was injured as a direct result of it` OR `I was injured trying to stop it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender`)
            `relationship to the primary victim who died`                                   IS `my relationship to the person who died`
            `had cohabited with the primary victim for at least 2 years`                    IS `I had lived with them as a de facto partner for at least 2 years`
            `was financially dependent on the primary victim immediately before the death`  IS `I was financially dependent on the person who died, immediately before the death`
            `was under 18 immediately before the death`                                     IS `I was under 18 immediately before the death`
            `was born after the death and would have been financially dependent`            IS `I was born after the death and would have been financially dependent on them`
            `has been given a recognition payment for another act in the same series`       IS `I have already been given a recognition payment for another act in the same series`
            `the act occurred after support was given for the earlier act`                  IS `this act happened after support was given for the earlier act`
            `has applied to the Tribunal for review of a decision about the recognition payment` IS `I have applied to the Tribunal for review of the decision about my recognition payment`
            `the Tribunal has ordered that the payment is not suspended`                    IS `the Tribunal has ordered that my payment is not suspended`)

§§ `ss 31 to 33, Regulation cl 5 to 8 -- my counselling`

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, how much counselling is paid for (Victims Rights and Support Regulation 2019 cl 5, 7)?
GIVEN `I am applying for counselling as` IS A `Counselling class` @desc Which you are: a primary or secondary victim; a family victim; a relevant family member (a relative of a person who died who is not a family victim); or none of these
      `whether I am a victim is still being worked out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has still to establish whether you are a victim, and counselling may help to establish it
      `my counselling is outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the counselling is provided outside Australia
      `my counsellor's hourly fee outside Australia` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars an hour: the fee of the counsellor you have chosen outside Australia (0 if the counselling is in Australia)
      `I am, or was while under 18, a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 and a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse, or were a victim of it while under 18
      `hours of counselling already paid for this act` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours of approved counselling already paid for in respect of this act (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Counselling answer`
`how much counselling is paid for` `I am applying for counselling as` `whether I am a victim is still being worked out` `my counselling is outside Australia` `my counsellor's hourly fee outside Australia` `I am, or was while under 18, a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse` `hours of counselling already paid for this act` MEANS
    `the counselling hours for`
        (`Counselling facts` WITH
            `counselling class`                                                       IS `I am applying for counselling as`
            `whether the person is a victim is still being established`               IS `whether I am a victim is still being worked out`
            `the counselling is provided outside Australia`                           IS `my counselling is outside Australia`
            `the counsellor's hourly fee outside Australia`                           IS `my counsellor's hourly fee outside Australia`
            `is, or was while under 18, a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse` IS `I am, or was while under 18, a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse`
            `hours of counselling already paid for the act`                           IS `hours of counselling already paid for this act`)

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, how much is paid for my approved counselling (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 33; Regulation cl 8)?
GIVEN `my counsellor is` IS A `Counsellor class` @desc Your counsellor: a generalist counsellor tier 1; a generalist counsellor tier 2 (a qualified psychologist or social worker with over 3 years' approved counselling and specialist skills, as the Commissioner sees it); or a psychiatrist
      `hours of counselling` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours of approved counselling provided
      `hours of my counsellor's travel period` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours of one period your counsellor spent travelling to counsel you (0 if none)
      `the GST payable` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the GST payable on the counselling
      `other costs the Commissioner has determined to be appropriate` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: any amount the Commissioner has determined to be appropriate for other costs of the counselling (0 if none)
      `I am resident in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are resident in Australia
GIVETH A `Counselling payment answer`
`how much is paid for my counselling` `my counsellor is` `hours of counselling` `hours of my counsellor's travel period` `the GST payable` `other costs the Commissioner has determined to be appropriate` `I am resident in Australia` MEANS
    `the cl 8 payment for`
        (`Counselling services` WITH
            `the counsellor`                                      IS `my counsellor is`
            `hours of counselling`                                IS `hours of counselling`
            `hours of the counsellor's travel period`             IS `hours of my counsellor's travel period`
            `GST payable`                                         IS `the GST payable`
            `costs the Commissioner determines to be appropriate` IS `other costs the Commissioner has determined to be appropriate`
            `the victim is resident in Australia`                 IS `I am resident in Australia`)

§§ `ss 38 to 40 -- making my application`

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, may I make an application for victims support (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 38)?
GIVEN `I am applying as` IS A `Capacity of the applicant` @desc Who you are: a victim of an act of violence or an act of modern slavery; a family victim of a road crime; a parent, step-parent or guardian of a primary victim who is a child; another person with a genuine interest in the victim's welfare, applying on the victim's behalf; or none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may I make an application` `I am applying as` MEANS
    `may apply for victims support as` `I am applying as`

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, what documentary evidence that s 39 asks for is missing from my application (an empty answer means nothing s 39 lists is missing; the approved form may ask for more) (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 39)?
GIVEN `the kind of support I am applying for` IS A `Kind of support applied for` @desc The kind of support: approved counselling services; financial assistance for immediate needs; for actual loss of earnings; for out-of-pocket expenses; for medical and dental expenses; for justice related expenses; for clothing and personal effects; funeral expenses; or a recognition payment
      `the class of victim I am applying as` IS A `Victim class` @desc The class of victim you are applying as: a primary victim; a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim; a secondary victim; a family victim of an act of violence; or a family victim of a road crime
      `I have a police report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a police report about the act
      `I have a report from a government agency or a victims support agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a report from a government agency, or from an agency funded by the State or the Commonwealth to support victims of crime
      `I have a medical, dental or counselling report verifying my injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a medical, dental or counselling report verifying that you (or the child who is the primary victim) were actually injured as a result of the act
      `I have receipts, invoices or other proof of the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have receipts, invoices or other approved proof of the expenses incurred or to be incurred
      `I have my employer's details and statement of my time off work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have your employer's name and address, the period you were off work and a statement from your employer confirming them
GIVETH A LIST OF `Missing evidence`
`what evidence is missing` `the kind of support I am applying for` `the class of victim I am applying as` `I have a police report` `I have a report from a government agency or a victims support agency` `I have a medical, dental or counselling report verifying my injury` `I have receipts, invoices or other proof of the expenses` `I have my employer's details and statement of my time off work` MEANS
    `the evidence s 39 asks for that is missing`
        (`Evidence facts` WITH
            `kind of support`                                                   IS `the kind of support I am applying for`
            `applying as`                                                       IS `the class of victim I am applying as`
            `has a police report`                                               IS `I have a police report`
            `has a report by a government agency or a victims support agency`   IS `I have a report from a government agency or a victims support agency`
            `has a medical, dental or counselling report verifying the injury`  IS `I have a medical, dental or counselling report verifying my injury`
            `has receipts, invoices or other substantiation of the expenses`    IS `I have receipts, invoices or other proof of the expenses`
            `has the employer's details and statement of the period off work`   IS `I have my employer's details and statement of my time off work`)

GIVEN `the kind of support I am applying for` IS A `Kind of support applied for`
      `the victim's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE
      `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day that was established` IS A DATE
      `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Application timing`
`my application timing from my answers` `the kind of support I am applying for` `the victim's date of birth` `the day it happened` `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it` `the day that was established` `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault` `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me` MEANS
    `Application timing` WITH
        `kind of support`                                                          IS `the kind of support I am applying for`
        `the victim's date of birth`                                               IS `the victim's date of birth`
        `the day the act occurred`                                                 IS `the day it happened`
        `is a family victim, and the cause of death was only established later`    IS `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it`
        `the day it was established that the death was a direct result of the act` IS `the day that was established`
        `the act involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault`        IS `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault`
        `is a primary victim of an act of violence in the course of a sexual offence against them` IS `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me`

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, by when must I apply for this kind of support (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 40(1) to (5), (7))?
GIVEN `the kind of support I am applying for` IS A `Kind of support applied for` @desc The kind of support: approved counselling services; financial assistance for immediate needs; for actual loss of earnings; for out-of-pocket expenses; for medical and dental expenses; for justice related expenses; for clothing and personal effects; funeral expenses; or a recognition payment
      `the victim's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (or that of the victim you are applying for), as YYYY-MM-DD
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the act occurred, as YYYY-MM-DD (for a series of related acts, the day you count from; the Act does not say which)
      `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a family victim: whether it was only established later (by a court or otherwise) that the person died as a direct result of the act
      `the day that was established` IS A DATE @desc The day it was established that the death was a direct result of the act, as YYYY-MM-DD (any date if it does not apply)
      `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault
      `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the primary victim and the act occurred in the course of a sexual offence against you
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`by when must I apply` `the kind of support I am applying for` `the victim's date of birth` `the day it happened` `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it` `the day that was established` `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault` `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me` MEANS
    `the time limit for` (`my application timing from my answers` `the kind of support I am applying for` `the victim's date of birth` `the day it happened` `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it` `the day that was established` `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault` `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me`)

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, is an application I make on this day in time (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 40)?
GIVEN `the day I make the application` IS A DATE @desc The day you make, or made, the application, as YYYY-MM-DD
      `the kind of support I am applying for` IS A `Kind of support applied for` @desc The kind of support: approved counselling services; financial assistance for immediate needs; for actual loss of earnings; for out-of-pocket expenses; for medical and dental expenses; for justice related expenses; for clothing and personal effects; funeral expenses; or a recognition payment
      `the victim's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (or that of the victim you are applying for), as YYYY-MM-DD
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the act occurred, as YYYY-MM-DD (for a series of related acts, the day you count from; the Act does not say which)
      `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a family victim: whether it was only established later (by a court or otherwise) that the person died as a direct result of the act
      `the day that was established` IS A DATE @desc The day it was established that the death was a direct result of the act, as YYYY-MM-DD (any date if it does not apply)
      `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault
      `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the primary victim and the act occurred in the course of a sexual offence against you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is my application in time` `the day I make the application` `the kind of support I am applying for` `the victim's date of birth` `the day it happened` `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it` `the day that was established` `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault` `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me` MEANS
    `an application made on` `the day I make the application` `is in time for` (`my application timing from my answers` `the kind of support I am applying for` `the victim's date of birth` `the day it happened` `I am a family victim and it was only established later that the death was a direct result of it` `the day that was established` `it involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault` `I am the primary victim, and it happened in the course of a sexual offence against me`)

@export Under the NSW Victims Support Scheme, can I still make claims under my application (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 s 40(6))?
GIVEN `the day I made my application` IS A DATE @desc The day your application for victims support was duly made, as YYYY-MM-DD
      `the day of my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make the claim, as YYYY-MM-DD
      `the total maximum financial support has been given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the total maximum amount of financial support you can receive for the act has already been given
GIVETH A `Claims answer`
`can I still make claims` `the day I made my application` `the day of my claim` `the total maximum financial support has been given to me` MEANS
    `whether claims may be made under an application made on` `the day I made my application` `on` `the day of my claim` `when` `the total maximum financial support has been given to me`
